Subject: [S] split-plot/repeated measures for multinomial data
Message-ID: <s6dae4ec.026@landcare.cri.nz>

Dear S-Plus users,

I have data from a multi-stratum study where the response is categorical:
each unit is classified as 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4 (0<1<...<4).  The design is
complicated.  The main sampling unit is an area to which a treatment is
applied.  Within each area transects are randomly sampled; within each
transect plots are sampled; and within each plot the units we measure
are selected and classified on several different occasions.

If the data were normal I could use aov() with appropriate error terms or
lme() to test for treatment and time effects.  Does anyone know of similar
functions in S-Plus for complicated mixed effects models when the
response is multinomial?  

Thanks

Ray Webster
