From Diego.Kuonen at epfl.ch  Mon Mar  1 22:11:45 1999
From: Diego.Kuonen at epfl.ch (Diego Kuonen)
Date: Mon, 01 Mar 1999 23:11:45 +0100
Subject: Re: [S] y2k problem in Splus
References: <9903012150.AA13631@vanryzin.cpmc.columbia.edu>
Message-ID: <36DB10A1.43689C79@epfl.ch>

"Dr. Heitjan" wrote:

> I am using Version 3.4 Release 1 for Sun SPARC, SunOS 5.3 : 1996
>
> Note the following:
>
> > dates(14609)
> [1] 12/31/99
> > dates(14610)
> [1] 01/01/100
>
> However, if we supply a more elaborate format, things work properly:
>
> > dates(14609,format='mm/dd/yy')
> [1] Dec/31/1999
> > dates(14610,format='mm/dd/yy')
> [1] Jan/01/2000
>
> Has anybody figured out a fix for this?

The problem comes from the functions dates() et seq.dates().
This only occurs with S-Plus 3.4 for UNIX...

To fix this, use the "out.format=" parameter as in the following example:

> dates(100, out.format="month day year",  origin=c(month=12,day=20,year=1999))
[1] March 29 2000

See also
http://www.mathsoft.com/press/y2k/splus.html

  Diego Kuonen

