In my continuing S-Plus education, I'm trying to manipulate data and
perform actions that are trivial in other statistics programs and computer
languages.

In English, here is what I'm trying to do:

mydataframe has a bunch of variables, two of which are sex and species.  I
have two sexes per species ("M" and "F") and 4 species ("A", "B", "C", and
"C").  The entire dataset has been imported from SAS and in the import, the
sex variable and the species variable have arrived as factors.

So, here is what I want to do:

if sex is "M" and species is "A" add the variable group to the dataframe
and number it 1.

if sex is "F" and species is "A" make the value of group 2.

etc so that I end up with a variable called group with eight possible
values ranging from 1 - 8.

Since sex and species are factors, I found that:

group<-paste(sex, species, sep='')
category(group)
mydataframe<-cbind(mydataframe, group)

does what I need, but surely there must be a more direct way to do this.
I've looked at the syntax of if() and ifelse() and have played a bit with
them, but neither seem to do precisely what I want.

Is there a recommended way to do this kind of manipulation?  I've looked at
VR2, Spector, the SPlus 4 manuals, and the Becker et al "Blue Book".  I
can't find an example -- my eyesight is failing (literally) -- so it is
possible I missed one.

