Marc,

There are two types of answers.

(1) To combine multiple variables for the purpose of cross-classification you
      can use the interaction() or paste() functions.

(2) For most purposes you don't actually need to combine them as you
     can cross-classify on the fly.  E.g.:

     tapply(age, list(sex,species), median, na.rm=T)
     Also: by, aggregate, etc. functions

     In Hmisc library: summarize(age, llist(sex,species), median, na.rm=T)
     to produce a new data frame of summary stats (suitable for trellis 
graphics).
     Also in Hmisc: summary(age ~ sex + species, fun=median) to do analyses
     separately by sex then species, or add method='cross' to cross-classify
     on them simultaneously.

-Frank Harrell

