you can use the group= argument

xyplot(y~x|panelfactor,group=grpfactor,panel=panel.superpose)

will do multiple plots of y vs x on the same panel with different
symbols for different levels of grpfactor. If you want control over the
symbols you  need to use trellis.par.get() and trellis.par.set().

Frank Harrell's hmisc library has a function xYplot that does some of
the work for you:

xYplot(y~x|panelfactor,group=grpfactor)

produces a similar plot but with the groups labelled.

