Subject: Summary: [S] y2k problem in Splus
Message-ID: <9903031309.AA14767@vanryzin.cpmc.columbia.edu>

Thanks to Jim Box and Diego Kuonen for pointing out the Splus y2k
statement:

        http://www.mathsoft.com/press/y2k/splus_criteria.html

Specifically, you want to look at the "Prior statement" of Dec. 12, 98.
It points out that this problem exists in 3.x but not in later versions.
The only fix suggested is to use the more elaborate format when printing
dates.  If you use the abbreviated format for years, 1999 is correctly
printed as '99' but 2000 is printed as '100'.
