Message-ID: <BB669656DAD6D01191AE0000F803200C01677EC7@msgpacpbs1.rhq.pac.dfo-mpo.gc.ca>

Charles Anderson wrote:

>Have any of the fisheries modelers out there developed S-Plus scripts to
estimate VPA, CAGEAN, or Collie and Sissenwine >models? Would you send me
any such scripts, and any associated documentation or scripts to plot
residuals, population >trajectories, etc

You may be able to handle VPA models and simple catch-at-age models within
S-Plus.  CAGEAN is a more complicated catch-at-age model that I would not
attempt to implement in S-Plus due to the lack (I think) of an effective
non-linear minimization routine for problems with 10s or 100s of parameters.
I have no idea what "Collie and Sissenwine" model you mean.

What I do is the following.  I use S-Plus in concert with a product called
AD ModelBuilder.  ADMB uses automatic differentiation with an efficient
function minimizer to achieve extremely fast function minimization.  It
easily handles problems with 100s  or 1000s of parameters.  ADMB output can
be read into S-Plus for subsequent manipulation or plotting.  I believe
recent versions of the product have the ability for direct import of ADMB
data structures into S-Plus, although I have not used this feature.  For
likelihood and Bayesian problems, the variance-covariance matrix and
standard errors of arbitrary functions of parameters are essentially a free
by-product of the minimization.

Information on AD ModelBuilder can be obtained at the following website:
http://otter-rsch.com

You will find a fisheries catch-at-age example in the documentation.  If you
are doing lots of highly parameterized non-linear models, then ADMB is well
worth learning.  Please note I have no financial interest in ADMB.

Hope it helps.

Rob Kronlund
Pacific Biological Station
Nanaimo, British Columbia

