On Sun, 7 Mar 1999, Haicheng Tang wrote:

> 
> Hi there,
> 
> Does anyone know how to track the time running
> an Splus program takes? I want to know this to 

Look at the clock window, or a process monitor such as top, wintop or task
manager? Or use proc.time or unix.time or dos.time in S-PLUS (which must be
obvious functions to look at from the help system).

> figure out how much time a big simulation program 
> will take by running a smaller version 1st.

Be warned that most people find the scaling is not linear due to memory
build up to a point at which paging slows things down.  A very common
mistake for our students is to time 10 runs of a bootstrap, find it takes 5
secs, then try to do 1000 and find this takes hours.  (A mistake, because
they are warned about this in their S-PLUS programming lecture.)

