Subject: [S] anova.manova?
Message-ID: <9903120732.ZM81480@pascal.math.yorku.ca>

Does anyone have a function that would, essentially, fulfill the role
of "anova.manova"?  That is, with two manova fits:

     >  fit1 <- manova(Y ~ x1 )

     >  fit2 <- manova(Y ~ x1 + x2 + x3)

you could get the standard tests (Pillai, etc.) for testing
fit1 against fit2 as the alternative.  Presumably, it would be called
anova.manova and would have the same optional arguments as 
summary.manova which allows you to test only a single terms added last
in a model formula.

Thank you,
Georges Monette

