From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Sun Mar 28 06:16:06 1999
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian D Ripley)
Date: Sun, 28 Mar 1999 07:16:06 +0100
Subject: Re: [S] Importing, Editing functions
In-Reply-To: <19990327175744.A740@Buddha>
References: <19990327175744.A740@Buddha>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.05.9903280707090.18128-100000@auk.stats>

On Sat, 27 Mar 1999, Lance Hoffmeyer wrote (in one long line):

> I am using S5 in Linux with ESS and am trying to import a function
             ^^  S-PLUS 5, I presume.
> I wrote in S4 Win95.  How can I do this?

Use dump() and source() or (better) data.dump() and data.restore().
See the help pages for details.  Each provides a platform-independent
representation of S(-PLUS) objects.

Going the other way needs a little more care: it is possible to have
S-PLUS 5 objects (even functions) that cannot be parsed in S-PLUS 3/4.
This is unlikely to happen without your deliberating using the new
features of S version 4.

S5: now there's a thought!

