Not necessarily in my experience (I was assuming one had read the manual
page to get as far as oldStyle=T). In fact that data.dump(, oldStyle=T)
core dumps on me frequently. However, if you can get it to work and if you
have a function that manipulates slots, you will not be able to read the
dumpdata correctly in S-PLUS 3.x, since @ will not parse. Similarly for
lots of other new-style constructs.

